#N canvas 0 50 1040 1280 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   minimoog~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 minimoog model d style monosynth;
#X text 30 86 three oscillators with six waveforms and six ranges each plus hard sync and a noise source go into a 24 db ladder filter with emphasis and contour. filter and loudness envelopes with a decay switch glide legato lfo and overload drive. mono., f 110;
#X text 30 166 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 210 three band-limited oscillators with six waveforms. oscillator 3 can run free as an lfo range or follow the keyboard., f 110;
#X text 30 260 the ladder filter has tanh saturation and self-oscillates. the mixer can overdrive it for the classic thick bass., f 110;
#X text 30 310 it is monophonic with a note stack: release a key and the synth goes back to the key still held., f 110;
#X text 30 350 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 394 1  open the engine page below and turn dsp on, f 110;
#X text 30 424 2  play a midi keyboard or click chord on, f 110;
#X text 30 454 3  open the parameters page and move any control or open presets and step through the sounds, f 110;
#X text 30 484 4  everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy, f 110;
#X text 30 544 try:  load fat bass: osc 2 sits a little off pitch and osc 3 is an octave below, f 110;
#X text 30 574 try:  set sync on and move tune2: the classic sync sweep, f 110;
#X text 30 604 try:  raise drive and res with a low cutoff for the thick overloaded sound, f 110;
#X text 30 648 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 692 no sound: turn dsp on in the engine page and check the volume slider. the synth needs a note: click chord on or play a midi key, f 110;
#X text 30 742 nothing changes after a rebuild: pd keeps the old external in memory so close every patch and restart pd, f 110;
#X text 30 772 a note is stuck: send panic. a missing note off from a midi device is the usual cause, f 110;
#X text 30 802 unknown parameter in the console: names are exact and lowercase so send params to print them all, f 110;
#X text 30 832 a bank file is not found: save and load names are relative to the folder of this patch, f 110;
#X text 30 862 the sliders do not move when you change a preset: the object must be created with the same name as in the boxes. default name is the object name, f 110;
#X text 30 912 clicks or dropouts: raise the audio buffer in the pd audio settings or lower the voice count in the creation argument, f 110;
#X text 30 962 a chord plays one note: the minimoog is monophonic so the last key wins, f 110;
#X text 30 992 range lo makes no pitch: lo is a low-frequency range used as an lfo, f 110;
#X text 30 1036 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 1242 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 presets: factory sounds are stored as plain text and every control above is a message. click a box to load that sound, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; minimoog preset 0;
#X text 250 112 0  fat bass;
#X msg 30 164 \; minimoog preset 1;
#X text 250 166 1  classic lead;
#X msg 30 218 \; minimoog preset 2;
#X text 250 220 2  sync screamer;
#X msg 30 272 \; minimoog preset 3;
#X text 250 274 3  pulse bass;
#X msg 30 326 \; minimoog preset 4;
#X text 250 328 4  hollow flute;
#X msg 30 380 \; minimoog preset 5;
#X text 250 382 5  brass section;
#X msg 30 434 \; minimoog preset 6;
#X text 250 436 6  squelch;
#X msg 460 110 \; minimoog preset 7;
#X text 680 112 7  zap tom;
#X msg 460 164 \; minimoog preset 8;
#X text 680 166 8  wobble;
#X msg 460 218 \; minimoog preset 9;
#X text 680 220 9  vibrato lead;
#X msg 460 272 \; minimoog preset 10;
#X text 680 274 10  wind;
#X msg 460 326 \; minimoog preset 11;
#X text 680 328 11  octave bass;
#X msg 460 380 \; minimoog preset 12;
#X text 680 382 12  soft triangle;
#X msg 460 434 \; minimoog preset 13;
#X text 680 436 13  pluck lead;
#X text 30 508 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 552 20 0 0 0 - minimoog-name - 0;
#X floatatom 230 552 4 0 0 0 - minimoog-index - 0;
#X text 340 554 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 596 \; minimoog next;
#X msg 190 596 \; minimoog prev;
#X msg 350 596 \; minimoog mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 656 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1, f 100;
#X text 30 706 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 750 \; minimoog A;
#X msg 166 750 \; minimoog B;
#X text 302 752 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 812 morph;
#X obj 110 810 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 minimoog-morph minimoog-morph-r empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 854 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every parameter blends smoothly between the two, f 100;
#X text 30 904 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 948 \; minimoog store mysound;
#X msg 262 948 \; minimoog save my.bank;
#X msg 486 948 \; minimoog load my.bank;
#X text 30 1008 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load adds the sounds from a text file, f 100;
#X text 30 1058 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 1102 every slider in the parameters page sends to minimoog-name and listens on minimoog-name-r so the stash library can store and morph whole scenes: create [stash/bank minimoog] and send it a scan message for a saved copy of the parameters page. this follows the stash naming rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 1080 pd presets;
#X text 30 1114 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1500 1824 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every control here is also a message: set name value with values from 0 to 1. switches take the step number shown under each one, f 120;
